1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 11=

3
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,000
Motive.

4
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,720
Give me a motive I can put in my report.

5
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,120
Don't tell me it was just
because you had an argument.

6
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:19,870
He laid a hand on my brother.

7
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:23,910
Our parents died when we were young.

8
00:01:25,870 --> 00:01:27,490
It's always been just the two of us.

9
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:29,870
Zi'an is...

10
00:01:32,270 --> 00:01:33,270
He's very innocent

11
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:34,760
and obedient.

12
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:39,000
But his health isn't very good.

13
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:40,800
He gets frightened easily.

14
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,080
I have to protect him.

15
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,910
Mr. Zhou.

16
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:56,000
Do me a favor.

17
00:01:56,190 --> 00:01:57,230
Lend me a wrench.

18
00:02:00,270 --> 00:02:01,230
Zi'an.

19
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,480
What are you taking pictures of?

20
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:03,680
What kind of photos are you taking?

21
00:02:04,630 --> 00:02:05,760
Let me have a look.

22
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,590
Let me see.

23
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:07,870
What are you photographing?

24
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:09,600
What's this?

25
00:02:14,880 --> 00:02:16,470
Wang Guoqiang

26
00:02:16,830 --> 00:02:18,190
never understood the meaning of

27
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:19,320
personal boundaries.

28
00:02:20,910 --> 00:02:22,320
I warned him.

29
00:02:22,320 --> 00:02:23,910
There's nothing here.

30
00:02:25,670 --> 00:02:27,270
The wrench is in the second box
by the door.

31
00:02:27,550 --> 00:02:28,190
Help yourself.

32
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,110
Take it and leave.

33
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:32,390
Look at you, being so protective.

34
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:34,520
All right.

35
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:36,000
I won't bother you two anymore.

36
00:02:36,190 --> 00:02:37,080
I'll leave you two alone.

37
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,000
You two.

38
00:02:38,390 --> 00:02:39,030
Zi'an.

39
00:02:39,320 --> 00:02:40,440
I'm going to get the wrench.

40
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:47,960
Are you okay?

41
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:49,600
He didn't touch you, did he?

42
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,830
Zicheng, you're hurting me.

43
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:00,320
As long as you're okay.

44
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,160
Remember.

45
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:03,190
Stay away from outsiders.

46
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,080
They don't understand you.

47
00:03:06,110 --> 00:03:07,520
They'll only hurt you.

48
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:12,800
That day,

49
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:15,630
he was drunk.

50
00:03:16,160 --> 00:03:18,320
He was saying nasty things
about my brother.

51
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:20,190
He called Zi'an a freak.

52
00:03:22,190 --> 00:03:24,440
He said neither of us was normal.

53
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,830
So you attacked him?

54
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,240
While he was talking,

55
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,720
he reached out to touch Zi'an's face.

56
00:03:33,110 --> 00:03:34,360
My brother was terrified.

57
00:03:34,390 --> 00:03:36,080
He was trembling with fear.

58
00:03:36,670 --> 00:03:37,360
So...

59
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,800
So I grabbed what I had in my hand

60
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:40,030
and struck him with it!

61
00:03:40,390 --> 00:03:41,720
I can't let anyone frighten him!

62
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:42,880
I can't let anyone touch him!

63
00:03:42,880 --> 00:03:44,080
He's all I have.

64
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:46,800
I have to protect him.

65
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,190
Do you understand?

66
00:03:57,390 --> 00:03:58,440
I killed him.

67
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:01,360
That's all.

68
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:04,800
Come in.

69
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:07,830
Captain Deng.

70
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:09,000
How's it going?

71
00:04:09,030 --> 00:04:09,880
What's up?

72
00:04:10,270 --> 00:04:10,800
I heard

73
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:12,390
you caught a suspect in that murder

74
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:13,800
in the urban village
a couple of days ago.

75
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,750
I thought I'd come take a look.

76
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,550
We're questioning him right now.

77
00:04:17,070 --> 00:04:18,110
He's been very cooperative.

78
00:04:18,510 --> 00:04:19,600
We barely had to ask anything

79
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,000
before he confessed to everything.

80
00:04:21,270 --> 00:04:22,790
He admitted he did it.

81
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:23,880
That simple?

82
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:26,760
It does seem a little too simple.

83
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,390
Speaking of which,

84
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,110
the dispatch center just reported

85
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:34,110
a burglary at a shop
in the urban village.

86
00:04:35,790 --> 00:04:37,320
Apparently, it's this man's shop.

87
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,920
Among the things
the burglars tried to steal,

88
00:04:39,920 --> 00:04:41,760
we found quite a few prohibited items.

89
00:04:41,950 --> 00:04:43,000
Most of them

90
00:04:43,350 --> 00:04:44,830
were smuggled surplus goods

91
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:46,390
from Cedar Group.

92
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:48,070
Come to think of it,

93
00:04:48,790 --> 00:04:50,550
there seems to be some connection

94
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,160
to the case you're investigating.

95
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,320
Yes.

96
00:04:53,720 --> 00:04:55,110
That's why I came to take a look.

97
00:04:56,110 --> 00:04:57,200
But

98
00:04:57,640 --> 00:04:58,790
there's still something suspicious.

99
00:04:59,640 --> 00:05:00,390
What is it?

100
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,230
When those petty thieves were caught,

101
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:05,200
they were reportedly sprawled
all over the shop.

102
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:07,230
There were also signs of a struggle.

103
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:08,200
A fight among themselves?

104
00:05:08,790 --> 00:05:09,640
Criminals turning on each other?

105
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:10,510
Possibly.

106
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:12,110
There were probably

107
00:05:12,110 --> 00:05:13,230
other people at the scene.

108
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,160
The strange thing is,

109
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:16,200
we checked all the surveillance footage

110
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:17,160
in that area.

111
00:05:17,440 --> 00:05:18,720
No one else was seen
entering or leaving.

112
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,040
Even the footage from nearby streets

113
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:22,160
had been altered.

114
00:05:25,270 --> 00:05:26,550
That is a little strange.

115
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:28,230
This method

116
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,000
feels somewhat

117
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:33,440
familiar.

118
00:05:34,320 --> 00:05:35,440
When Song Yang escaped,

119
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:37,070
he deleted the surveillance footage
the same way.

120
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:47,790
It's all been erased.

121
00:05:47,790 --> 00:05:48,550
It's okay.

122
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:50,920
You're safe for now.

123
00:05:51,070 --> 00:05:51,790
Is everyone okay?

124
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:52,390
We're fine.

125
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:53,510
Ada.

126
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:54,880
You need to be careful
around Zhou Zi'an.

127
00:05:55,390 --> 00:05:56,600
I have a feeling

128
00:05:57,110 --> 00:05:58,790
his relationship with Zhou Zicheng

129
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:01,000
isn't as simple as we thought.

130
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,200
Where am I?

131
00:06:17,040 --> 00:06:17,790
Senior.

132
00:06:19,390 --> 00:06:20,550
Why were you

133
00:06:20,550 --> 00:06:21,600
at my brother's shop today?

134
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:24,200
Zi'an.

135
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:25,070
Let me explain.

136
00:06:25,110 --> 00:06:26,110
Who are you really?

137
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:27,600
I thought we were friends.

138
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:28,950
Why did you lie to me?

139
00:06:29,110 --> 00:06:30,350
I consider you a friend, too.

140
00:06:30,390 --> 00:06:31,390
Please calm down.

141
00:06:31,920 --> 00:06:32,790
Then tell me.

142
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,390
Where exactly is my brother?

143
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:36,390
I saw the police take him away

144
00:06:36,480 --> 00:06:38,200
outside the shop this afternoon.

145
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:46,000
I haven't had a chance
to thank you, Senior.

146
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:47,320
Thank you for saving me.

147
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,270
I'm sorry.

148
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:49,550
I got too upset.

149
00:06:51,270 --> 00:06:52,200
Do you know

150
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:53,390
why my brother

151
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:54,640
was taken away?

152
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,320
Zhou Zicheng is suspected of involvement

153
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,070
in a murder two nights ago.

154
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:02,200
Impossible.

155
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,200
He was with me that night.

156
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,480
Then what exactly happened?

157
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:07,880
Can you tell me about it?

158
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:09,270
Maybe I can help him.

159
00:07:11,200 --> 00:07:12,390
Two nights ago...

160
00:07:20,110 --> 00:07:23,320
I... I can't remember.

161
00:07:23,480 --> 00:07:24,640
I just know

162
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,600
he didn't kill anyone.

163
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,390
He didn't.

164
00:07:33,880 --> 00:07:34,640
Senior.

165
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:37,830
Why are you here?

166
00:07:39,110 --> 00:07:41,270
Aren't you studying photography
at Hua University?

167
00:07:41,950 --> 00:07:43,720
I even took some nice photos of you.

168
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:48,480
What are you doing here?

169
00:07:50,270 --> 00:07:51,270
Be careful, Ada.

170
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:54,550
Zhou Zi'an may have some kind
of mental disorder.

171
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,350
Or...

172
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,110
Or he might be...

173
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,440
What are you doing here?

174
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:08,790
Why?

175
00:08:09,600 --> 00:08:10,670
Did you approach me

176
00:08:10,950 --> 00:08:12,600
to hurt my brother?

177
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,350
Zi'an.

178
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,600
Do you know you're an android?

179
00:08:22,200 --> 00:08:23,160
What are you talking about?

180
00:08:37,400 --> 00:08:38,150
Ada.

181
00:08:38,790 --> 00:08:40,640
How could I be an android?

182
00:08:56,790 --> 00:08:58,670
No wonder I felt
such a connection with you.

183
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:00,910
We're the same kind.

184
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,150
There's nothing wrong
with being an android.

185
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:08,030
But we need to find out

186
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:10,200
why you've been living as a human.

187
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,550
That's the mystery we need to solve,

188
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:13,200
Zi'an.

189
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:18,640
When we were little, Zicheng

190
00:09:18,790 --> 00:09:20,230
used to sneak me out to play.

191
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:21,400
After our parents died,

192
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,350
he paid for my education.

193
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,150
These memories are all so vivid.

194
00:09:32,150 --> 00:09:32,880
Ada.

195
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:34,280
Zhou Zi'an has mentioned

196
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:35,710
having confused memories several times.

197
00:09:36,470 --> 00:09:37,200
I think

198
00:09:37,200 --> 00:09:38,350
the answer we're looking for

199
00:09:38,400 --> 00:09:40,200
might be in that memory module.

200
00:09:49,400 --> 00:09:50,200
(Song Yang.)

201
00:09:50,710 --> 00:09:52,230
I need you to keep an eye on Zi'an.

202
00:09:53,230 --> 00:09:54,670
I'm reading the data now.

203
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:55,710
Okay.

204
00:09:55,710 --> 00:09:57,840
Connecting to
your information processing center.

205
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:09,140
(Cedar R&D Department 1)

206
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,880
Zi'an, I'm home.

207
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:27,000
Is dinner ready?

208
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,150
I'm starving.

209
00:10:28,150 --> 00:10:29,200
Go wash your hands.

210
00:10:29,790 --> 00:10:30,200
Zi'an.

211
00:10:31,590 --> 00:10:32,640
My teacher praised me again today

212
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,910
for having a talent for programming.

213
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:35,230
He also said I'd definitely

214
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:36,590
have a future in AI.

215
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,440
That's great.

216
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,590
Wonderful.

217
00:10:38,710 --> 00:10:39,760
Speaking of which,

218
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:40,640
Zi'an,

219
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:43,200
I want to enter

220
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,550
a robotics competition.

221
00:10:44,960 --> 00:10:46,550
Do we still have enough money?

222
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,200
Cheng.

223
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:51,790
Money isn't something you need
to worry about.

224
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,280
Someday,

225
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:54,910
when you become a master programmer,

226
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,350
I'll be your personal photographer.

227
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,150
Zi'an.

228
00:10:59,470 --> 00:11:00,590
Don't worry.

229
00:11:01,110 --> 00:11:02,350
When I grow up,

230
00:11:02,710 --> 00:11:04,470
I'll make sure you have a good life.

231
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:14,140
(Cedar R&D Department 1)

232
00:11:14,150 --> 00:11:16,150
Impressive work, Zicheng.

233
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:17,520
Ms. Shen was just saying

234
00:11:17,520 --> 00:11:18,840
your optimization algorithm

235
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,350
is the work of a genius.

236
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,350
I think you've got a good chance
of getting hired permanently.

237
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:24,520
Not really.

238
00:11:24,670 --> 00:11:26,030
I still have a lot to learn.

239
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:35,230
Hello?

240
00:11:35,230 --> 00:11:36,000
(Hello.)

241
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:38,200
(Is this Mr. Zhou Zicheng?)

242
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:41,000
(This is the morgue at
the Third Municipal People's Hospital.)

243
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:42,520
(We've just received)

244
00:11:42,520 --> 00:11:44,200
(a victim of a traffic accident.)

245
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:45,320
(Mr. Zhou Zi'an.)

246
00:11:45,550 --> 00:11:47,280
(You're listed
as his emergency contact.)

247
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:50,350
Hello?

248
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:52,440
Mr. Zhou Zicheng?

249
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,030
Are you still there?

250
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:55,760
Hello?

251
00:12:53,790 --> 00:12:54,960
Zi'an.

252
00:12:58,280 --> 00:13:01,080
We're about to have a better life.

253
00:13:03,470 --> 00:13:05,150
Why?

254
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,400
Zi'an.

255
00:13:10,150 --> 00:13:11,790
Why?

256
00:13:29,670 --> 00:13:30,440
Zi'an.

257
00:13:31,590 --> 00:13:32,400
I gave you

258
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,000
some of my memories.

259
00:13:42,400 --> 00:13:43,710
From now on,

260
00:13:44,590 --> 00:13:45,880
I'm the older brother,

261
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:47,640
and you're the younger brother.

262
00:13:49,150 --> 00:13:50,880
It's my turn to protect you.

263
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,590
My goodness.

264
00:14:08,790 --> 00:14:10,670
Zhou Zicheng is out of his mind.

265
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,790
He's also a genius.

266
00:14:13,320 --> 00:14:14,710
He stripped Zhou Zi'an of almost

267
00:14:14,710 --> 00:14:16,550
all his android functions

268
00:14:16,760 --> 00:14:17,880
just to make him appear

269
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,230
more human.

270
00:14:19,710 --> 00:14:20,400
Ada.

271
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:22,470
He fooled both of us.

272
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:24,710
But this module seems to contain

273
00:14:24,710 --> 00:14:26,320
Zhou Zicheng's memories.

274
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,590
Yes.

275
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:41,760
(AGENT CONSOLE)
He edited his own memories

276
00:14:42,110 --> 00:14:43,840
(to create an entirely
new set of memories.)

277
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:45,880
(He also developed
a complete backstory,)

278
00:14:45,880 --> 00:14:47,710
(personality traits,
and humanlike thought patterns.)

279
00:14:48,110 --> 00:14:50,080
Together, they formed
the younger brother we know,

280
00:14:50,280 --> 00:14:51,280
Zhou Zi'an.

281
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:53,640
Ada.

282
00:14:53,710 --> 00:14:55,000
I need more data.

283
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,280
Zi'an.

284
00:15:00,670 --> 00:15:02,030
To find out the truth,

285
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:03,280
I need to run

286
00:15:03,280 --> 00:15:04,230
some diagnostic checks on you.

287
00:15:04,230 --> 00:15:05,110
Would that be okay?

288
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:09,550
Will it hurt?

289
00:15:09,790 --> 00:15:10,760
No, it won't.

290
00:16:04,110 --> 00:16:11,390
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

291
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:17,090
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

292
00:16:17,130 --> 00:16:20,000
♪That's me, too♪

293
00:16:21,540 --> 00:16:25,060
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

294
00:16:25,890 --> 00:16:29,360
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

295
00:16:29,980 --> 00:16:33,770
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

296
00:16:34,090 --> 00:16:36,620
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

297
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:41,220
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

298
00:16:41,220 --> 00:16:43,350
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

299
00:16:43,350 --> 00:16:46,520
♪Bring me something more?♪

300
00:16:47,220 --> 00:16:53,950
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

301
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:58,180
♪Sadness is blue♪

302
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:02,400
♪How would you paint me?♪

303
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:07,130
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

304
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:09,390
♪Painting without restraint♪

305
00:17:09,580 --> 00:17:12,170
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

306
00:17:12,170 --> 00:17:16,360
♪If I could start over♪

307
00:17:16,530 --> 00:17:20,430
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

308
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:23,180
♪Give me back my smile♪

309
00:17:23,780 --> 00:17:26,260
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

310
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:32,000
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
